Review written to `docs/reviews/python-gaps/pygap-04-python-metrics-bindings.md`.

**Summary**: 8 findings — 1 high, 3 medium, 4 low.

| # | Severity | Area | Issue |
|---|----------|------|-------|
| 1 | high | NaN/inf | No guards on power values; NaN propagates silently through all accumulators |
| 2 | medium | Monthly summaries | Not implemented |
| 3 | medium | LDC | Not implemented |
| 4 | medium | Annual totals | `total` is net energy, not gross consumption — misleading for PV homes |
| 5 | low | Peak demand | `ceil()` overestimates rolling window for non-divisible timesteps |
| 6 | low | Gas/therm constant | `29.3001` vs physics constant `29.3071` (~0.024% discrepancy) |
| 7 | low | Python exposure | `total_consumption_kwh`, `total_pv_generation_kwh_abs`, `combined_annual_energy_kwh()` not exposed |
| 8 | low | Energy cost | Cost lives in `TariffTelemetry`, not `SimulationMetrics` — no duplicate calculation |

Areas without issues: unit consistency (no J-to-kWh factor to get wrong), off-by-one timestep (all rows processed), and return types (`.pyi` stubs are complete and correct).
